{
  "name": "Daily social digest: what people post about your topic, summarized to Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "n1",
      "name": "Every morning",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "days",
              "triggerAtHour": 8
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "name": "Search posts on Reddit and TikTok",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-juicer.juicer",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "socialData",
        "operation": "searchPosts",
        "term": "your brand",
        "platforms": [
          "Reddit",
          "TikTok"
        ],
        "termType": "mentions",
        "limit": 25
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "id": "n3",
      "name": "Combine posts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.aggregate",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "aggregate": "aggregateAllItemData",
        "destinationFieldName": "posts",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n4",
      "name": "Summarize",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
      "position": [
        880,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a social media analyst. Below are recent social posts about our topic as JSON. Write a short Slack digest: 3 to 5 themes people talk about, the overall mood, and the 3 posts most worth reading with their links. Plain text, no tables.\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.posts.map(post => ({ platform: post.platform, author: post.poster?.name, text: (post.message || '').slice(0, 400), url: post.url, likes: post.like_count }))) }}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n5",
      "name": "OpenAI model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        880,
        220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-4o-mini"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n6",
      "name": "Post to Slack",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        1180,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "select": "channel",
        "channelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "#social-digest"
        },
        "text": "={{ $json.text }}",
        "otherOptions": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n7",
      "name": "How it works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 380,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Daily social digest\nEvery morning Juicer searches Reddit and TikTok for your keyword in one call, a Code step keeps posts from the last 2 days that really mention it, the AI model summarizes the themes and mood, and the digest lands in Slack.\n\n**Set up**\n1. Add your Juicer API key (Developer page in Juicer).\n2. Change the term and platforms in the Juicer node. Use a #hashtag with Term Type Hashtag for X, Instagram, LinkedIn or YouTube.\n3. Connect OpenAI and Slack.\n\n**Cost:** each platform spends Juicer API credits per run (Reddit 1, TikTok 3)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n8",
      "name": "Keep recent on-topic posts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Keep posts from the last 2 days that actually mention the keyword.\n// Change the keyword to match the term in the Juicer node.\nconst keyword = 'your brand';\nconst since = Date.now() - 2 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\n\nreturn $input.all().filter(item =>\n  (item.json.message || '').toLowerCase().includes(keyword.toLowerCase()) &&\n  new Date(item.json.post_created_at).getTime() >= since,\n);"
      }
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Every morning": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
